WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.999
Swords in one piece have a will of their own,
that needs to be tamed by its wielder, which

00:00:05.999 --> 00:00:12.720
is the key to Zoro's next step in becoming
the strongest swordsman in the world.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.120
We have to talk about swords.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:20.180
So the power system in one piece is...weird
for lack of a better term.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:25.190
The main thing used to be Devil fruits, that
we have discussed in depth recently, and then

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:30.480
Haki was introduced as a counter weight but
at the same time enhancement to the devil

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.680
fruit system.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:37.160
That system is luckily starting to make more
and more sense, but it sure is a bit confusing,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.860
probably on purpose.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.550
Like I'm 85.4% sure it's on purpose.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:48.290
Point is, if you don't have a devil fruit,
you can still become ridiculously strong by

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:53.310
being a powerful Haki user.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:01:02.450
However, you don't ever see anyone without
a devil fruit simply fighting with their body--except

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.740
Sanji, he is literally the only person I could
think of that doesn't use a weapon, though

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.680
he technically is a human weapon himself.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.579
So given the latest developments in the manga,
and yes this video will contain some spoilers

00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:21.999
for Zoro, I want to talk about the third and
least-discussed part of the one piece power

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:25.710
system: Weapons.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:32.100
Hi my name is Manu, I keep wanting to buy
a katana, even though I don't have space left

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:37.479
in my room and today we're gonna address the
latest reveal around swords in One Piece,

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:43.709
what it actually means to create a black blade
and why Zoro has now reached the next level

00:01:43.709 --> 00:01:44.709
as a swordsman.

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:49.189
Also, I know you already get this, but for
the few people who seem to be confused about

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:54.859
this: I tend to start my videos with an analysis
fully based on the material and then end it

00:01:54.859 --> 00:01:55.859
with some theorising.

00:01:55.859 --> 00:02:00.299
I just personally like to think about what
things could look like in the future.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:04.240
So: Swords have a special place in my heart
as a one piece fan.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.550
Many of the most legendary characters in the
story are swordsman.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:14.959
Zoro, Brook, Mihawk, the Samurai of Wano such
as Ryuma or Oden, Whitebeard, Shanks, Rayleigh

00:02:14.959 --> 00:02:23.040
and even Roger himself.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.651
On the surface one might think that swords
are nothing but tools, that pirates use, no

00:02:27.651 --> 00:02:29.890
matter if strong or weak.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:35.209
But since Luffy luckily has a man in his crew
that aims to become the strongest swordsman

00:02:35.209 --> 00:02:40.040
in the world, we do know that there is much
much more to these weapons than meets the

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.040
eye.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.379
After all Oda went through the trouble of
introducing a whole grading system for swords,

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:52.319
with countless regular grad swords, 49 Skillful
grade swords, 21 great grade swords, that's

00:02:52.319 --> 00:02:56.430
funny to say, as well as the 12 supreme grade
swords.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:02.079
Each of these grades or meito in Japanese
tell us something about the quality, history

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:04.170
and power of a blade.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:09.739
Mihawk's Yoru and Whitebeaerd's Murakumogiri
for instance are part of that exclusive dozen.

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:14.900
Now interestingly enough there are two philosophies
in the one piece world that at first glance

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.090
seem to oppose each other.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:22.780
On the one hand we have Mihawk, who holds
the title of strongest swordsman in the world

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:27.430
and thus undoubtedly one of the strongest
characters in the series.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:32.659
While training Zoro during the time skip,
as he teaches him about Haki, Mihawk tells

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:42.239
us the following about black blades: [every
sword can be a black blade]

00:03:42.239 --> 00:03:45.099
The idea behind this is pretty straight-forward
I think.

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:50.359
It doesn't matter if you wield a supreme grade
sword or a kitchen knife, if you are a true

00:03:50.359 --> 00:04:00.620
master of the sword, any blade becomes a powerful
weapon, as Zoro nicely demonstrates here [Zoro

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:10.530
uses the small seppuku knife].

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:16.450
The sword is nothing but a tool that depends
on the skill of its wielder.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:21.000
After arriving in Wano however, I couldn't
help but realise that the philosophy of the

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.130
samurai here was quite the opposite.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:30.190
Swords and their names held extreme meaning
here and were talked about almost like human

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.190
beings.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:36.260
Shusui is regarded as much of a national treasure
as Ryuma himself.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:41.660
Tenguyama tells us about the nature of the
3 Kitetsu blades and then we get introduced

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:51.230
to Enma, Oden's old sword, that immediately
starts draining Zoro's power.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:59.970
It became clear that certain blades actually
harbour certain abilities.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:05.670
Enma clearly takes its users haki and channels
it into attacks of amplified power.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:11.490
So again, the border between sword and swordsman
became a bit more complicated.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:16.350
Certain swords have certain powers, but then
again, what about brook's ice attacks?

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.610
Is that his skill or his sword?

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:19.950
Or Kinemon's fire-cutting?

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:25.660
He taught that to Zoro, so it seems to be
a skill that can be done with any sword.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:32.830
What I'm saying is, just like Haki or devil
fruits, Swords in one piece are just as complicated.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.120
Which one is more important now Mr. Mihawk,
Skill or Sword?

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.490
I mean you run around with one of the 12 most
infamous blades in the world?

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:45.860
But the truth is of course, that I don't think
Mihawk is wrong with what he told Zoro.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:50.830
Mihawk knows that a good swordsman needs to
be subscribed to my channel for next generation

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:57.080
anime content, that, and that a great sword
makes a big difference, that's why he decides

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:06.830
to use Yoru, after acknowledging Zoro[].

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:12.761
Mihawk is emphasising skill over blade during
Zoro's training for two reasons: First, this

00:06:12.761 --> 00:06:17.830
lesson is about Haki and coating one's sword,
so it doesn't get damaged.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:22.490
It's about Zoro learning to make any weapon
as deadly and effective as possible.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:28.620
But secondly, Mihawk knows that without reaching
enormous proficiency as a swordsman, you can't

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.990
even hope to use the benefits of a special
sword, such as Yoru.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:39.750
Zoro is already immensely powerful, more powerful
a fighter than the scabbards, who are considered

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.300
strong even among the strong people of Wano.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:50.060
And still, he is barely able to keep Enma
from sucking out all his power or doing what

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.180
he wants.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:57.500
Truly special swords require skill on the
highest level, so fo Mihawk, the priority

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:03.030
in teaching Zoro was increasing his own power,
instead of telling him about the benefits

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:04.350
of a great swords.

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:09.020
By the way, quick question to my Spanish speaking
audience, cause I've always wondered, Mihawk

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:12.440
is supposed to be a Spanish inquisitor, right?

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:15.880
Like that's the vibe I get from his looks.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:20.580
Anyways, now with Zoro's fight against King
and his flashback back to his time at Shimotsuki

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.640
village, a lot of things have been cleared
up.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:28.090
Also, I just need to say how much I loved
that flashback in general.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:33.390
I can like never get enough of the story connecting
us back to the beginnings and giving us more

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.390
context.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:39.230
Anyways, we see Zoro's interaction with an
old man at the village, who turns out to be

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:45.460
Shimotsuki Kozaburo, the legendary smith,
who illegally left Wano and founded the Dojo

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:58.040
in the east blue, even though Zoro didn't
realise it at the time.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.650
He was the one that forged Enma for Oden.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:05.060
And he teaches us a lot about swords in just
a few panels.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:08.700
Together with Zoro we start piecing things
together.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:13.170
Kozaburo teaches us 3 very important things
about named swords.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:18.150
First, and this is maybe the most important
one, each graded blade has its own sort of

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.760
personality and power.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.890
Second, good swords choose their wielder and
wait for the right person.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:29.140
There are no cursed blades, it's just that
wielders of strong swords can't live up to

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:30.390
the swords standards.

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:35.099
And third, a powerful sword must be bent to
the swordsman's will and tamed.

00:08:35.099 --> 00:08:38.270
That is an awful lot of information dump we
got there.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:44.229
And as a quick caveat to all that, I want
to say that Kozaburo might not be the most

00:08:44.229 --> 00:08:50.490
reliable source, since his idea that swords
are only meant to kill seems not very Oda-like

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:51.490
to me.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:56.480
I think you agree that as Gandalf put it,
a swords true purpose should be to keep a

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.000
life, not to take one.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.650
And since we learned that Shimotsuki village
was founded by pirates, who knows what Kozaburo

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:06.640
was up to or who he was sailing with 50 years
ago.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:07.640
*Rocks*

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:12.910
That being said, he IS one of best, if not
the best swords smith we have met in the story,

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:16.640
who forged both Enma AND the Wano Ichimonji.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:20.030
So while I think that Zoro will come to a
different conclusion when it comes to a swords

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:25.480
true purpose, he most likely is right when
it comes to these other things.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:28.430
And that has huge implications.

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:31.690
Like Nami's mysterious increase in bra-size
huge.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:35.150
This is beside the point, but does anyone
else prefer her original design?

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:41.200
Anyways, the fact that Swords are in some
way or form alive is an incredible reveal.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:44.730
Not exactly out of the blue, but incredible
nonetheless.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:50.450
The idea that objects can come to life from
a close and emotional bond with a person is

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.050
not new in One Piece.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:10:04.830
The going merry and its spirit are the most
prominent example I guess.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:09.770
And similarly it seems that a truly good sword
that is forged with passion and care by a

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:15.020
skilled craftsman also gets some sort of spirit
breathed into it.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:19.741
This is now partly speculation, but I think
it is founded really well in what we know

00:10:19.741 --> 00:10:21.020
about swords by now.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:25.391
The stronger the swords will, the stronger
its power seems to be, but it also means that

00:10:25.391 --> 00:10:29.670
it becomes harder to control and tame by its
wielder.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:35.170
While many regular swordsmen were not able
to control the sandai Kitetsu, Zoro was already

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:37.529
good enough to wield it.

00:10:37.529 --> 00:10:47.710
He felt the sword and passed its test[].

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:53.862
Enma however is on a completely different
level, which is why Zoro is struggling a lot

00:10:53.862 --> 00:10:55.010
with it at first.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:59.000
Now at this point, where I want to talk about
Zoro's next step as a swordsman, I would like

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:03.830
to draw an important distinction between two
things: Given all the information we have

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:09.750
right now, I strongly believe that being able
to control a powerful sword is not the same

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.370
as turning a sword into a black blade.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:17.110
Zoro comments on how Oden was able to wield
Enma with ease.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:22.670
However, despite fighting the likes of Roger
and Whitebeard on a regular basis, Oden never

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:25.010
turned Enma into a black blade.

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:27.840
Meanwhile Ryuma and Mihawk did.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:34.260
The trick to controlling a powerful 'cursed'
blade as Kozaburo says taming it and bending

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.630
it to your will.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:44.500
That immediately reminded me of all the times
Luffy used his haki to tame wild beasts.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:50.590
[] And it's conquerors haki that he uses.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:55.920
Similarly, when Zoro finally surrenders his
haki to Enma, suddenly his conquerors haki

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.290
bursts out.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:12:01.050
Enma literally is training Zoro to use conquerors
haki.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:05.029
And I think that's what it takes to control
a sword of Enma's kind.

00:12:05.029 --> 00:12:09.721
Looking at many of the other most powerful
swordsman, like Roger, Shanks, Rayleigh, WHitebeard

00:12:09.721 --> 00:12:15.010
or Oden, all of them had conquerors haki.

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:22.970
And I think for all these monsters, their
weapons is able to bundle their crazy haki

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:26.350
and make it a lot more efficient.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:30.750
Similarly to how luffy is learning to coat
himself in conquerors haki, I think Zoro will

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.200
have to learn that as well.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:37.779
Kaido for instance is clearly doing it when
he knocks Luffy unconscious with his thunder

00:12:37.779 --> 00:12:56.470
bagua, not because of the damage but because
he overwhelmed luffy.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:13:00.180
Or whitebeard and roger's blades don't touch.

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:06.380
That I believe is Zoro's next step, taming
Enma and earning it's loyalty.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:10.740
After that however, the question of course
will be wether Zoro will be able to turn his

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:12.800
blades into black blades.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:18.980
The answer if of course yes, but what exactly
does he need to do that?

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:24.680
Now my personal opinion is that a black swords
is quite similar to an awakened devil fruit.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:30.440
You have to fully master the sword and it's
individual personality to unlock its true

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:31.620
potential.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:36.120
But even more so, Zoro has to form a true
bond with his swords.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:41.460
They are important to him, yes, but he has
to get to know each of their personalities

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:47.589
and form a true relationship with them in
order to do what only true sword masters are

00:13:47.589 --> 00:13:48.589
capable of.

00:13:48.589 --> 00:13:52.620
And speaking of awakening, if you want to
learn more about that topic and what luffy's

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:57.120
next step will look like, I recommend you
check out that video, right here.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:58.480
What are you doing?

00:13:58.480 --> 00:13:59.570
Go watch it.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:00.570
Go.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.759
Go go go.

